<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">ISM is a long-established wholesaler of safety shoes and workwear. Its established retailer brand “Albatros” — used mainly for safety shoes, but also for workwear — suffered from a lack of esteem in the target group. The brand looked too much like a private label and therefore could not achieve adequate pricing.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The word mark “Albatros” was already established and known in the market — it was not up for debate. Besides the name, the logo contained only one other meaningful element: a globe. That association, however, was misleading — it suggests travel clothing rather than safety shoes, and above all it looks generic.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">From the globe to the wing</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Instead of the globe, the wing of the albatross — in a highly reduced form — moves to the fore as the defining brand element. This link to the brand heritage conveys durability, stamina and resilience — values as central to occupational safety as they are to the bird that gives the brand its name.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-1">The strongest promise a workwear brand can make is the functionality of its products.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">This gave rise to the new slogan: “Powered by Function.” While competitors in the segment bet on design and trends, Albatros deliberately sets itself apart through what actually matters to the core target group — functionality.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
